Whole English words and nord are strong cues; reaching the nort-/nord-
root over a token boundary is stronger still.  北 means north, including
when its UTF-8 bytes are split.  North compounds are weaker, and a few
geographical phrases retain a smaller response on the following word.
Unrelated small activations are left at zero.
