"""Component layers.1.mlp.down_proj:3239: a "first token of a segment" detector.

What it does. Inside a document the component is almost silent. It speaks only at the
first token of a segment, meaning the first token of a row, or the first token after
<|endoftext|>. There the model has no earlier text to look back on, so the component's
value is set by which token it is, and the sign follows the language of that token:

  German (and some Dutch) words          strongly negative (about -8)
  first names / name-like capitals       strongly positive (about +8)
  Cyrillic, Arabic, Katakana             positive (about +4)
  special chat tokens such as <|im_start|>  about +2.6
  ordinary Latin words after a space     mildly positive (+2)
  other Latin fragments                  about +1
  Hangul                                 slightly negative (-2)
  digits                                 slightly negative (-1)
  punctuation and blanks                 0

Everywhere else the program predicts 0. Only the token itself is used, since the first
token of a segment is the only token the model sees at that position.

